/* Every tunable number in one place, so playtesting changes are a one-line edit and a relaunch. Times are in
milliseconds and distances in tiles. Later sections add their own values here (surfaces, ledges, gaps, jump, duck,
mines and life costs). */

// The belt: the step interval starts here and shrinks by speedup_amount every speedup_period, never below min_step_time.
const int start_step_time = 500;
const int speedup_period = 10000;
const int speedup_amount = 10;
const int min_step_time = 50; // the top speed cap (dev, 2026-11-02: was 50, then 100, now back to 50)

/* Surfaces: the ground switches to a new random platform after a random stretch of running between these times, at any
speed (dev, 2026-11-03, for 1.1; it used to be 50 to 200 tiles, which took 25 to 100 s at 500 ms). */
const int surface_min_time = 10000;
const int surface_max_time = 20000; // 10 to 20 s (dev, 2026-11-03; first 30 s)

// Jumping: rise one height every jump_tick up to jump_height, then fall back the same way (about a second in the air).
const int jump_height = 5;
const int jump_tick = 100;

// Crouching: holding Down crouches, and it stands up on its own after duck_time even if Down is still held.
const int duck_time = 1500;
// After standing up, crouching is blocked for duck_cooldown, so Down can't be spammed (dev, 2026-11-03, for 1.1; was 1000).
const int duck_cooldown = 500;

/* Obstacle placement. An obstacle appears spawn_ahead_time before its countdown starts, at the current speed, so you
always hear it that long before its countdown begins. Spacing is built from a random stretch of normal floor between
one obstacle's ledge after and the next one's countdown (min_floor_time to max_floor_time below), never under
min_gap_tiles. */
const int spawn_ahead_time = 3000;
// The forward belt (dev, 2026-11-04): every belt sound drops a decibel for each belt_fade_ms of running away from you, at any speed.
const int belt_fade_ms = 150;
const int min_gap_tiles = 6;

/* The warning countdown before every trap: always countdown_length steps, warn1 to warn5, one cue per step, at any
speed (dev, 2026-11-03, for 1.1; it used to shrink with speed, 5 at 500 ms down to 1 at 100 ms). A jump lasts about
1 s, so at slow speeds you still jump on the last cues. A hazard's ledge before covers exactly the countdown; the
other traps count down on normal floor. A hazard's ledge after is a fixed ledge_after_tiles. */
const int countdown_length = 5;
const int ledge_after_tiles = 2;
// Normal floor between one obstacle and the next one's countdown: a random min_floor_time to max_floor_time at the current speed, never under min_floor_tiles.
const int min_floor_time = 1000;
const int max_floor_time = 4000;
const int min_floor_tiles = 2;
/* Difficulty (the game menu refactor plan, dev, 2026-11-05), one entry per level in difficulty_names' order: the
starting step time (the speed-up is the same for everyone), and the floor between obstacles, which stays fixed all run.
Chaos's floor is the min_floor_time to max_floor_time above, which debug and practice runs keep. */
const string[] difficulty_names = {"easy", "medium", "hard", "insane", "chaos"};
const int[] difficulty_start_times = {500, 450, 400, 350, 300};
const int[] difficulty_min_floor_times = {2000, 1750, 1500, 1250, 1000};
const int[] difficulty_max_floor_times = {5000, 4750, 4500, 4250, 4000};
/* Damage by level (the difficulty scaling plan, dev, 2026-11-09: "I like option 2 much better"): the percent of every
obstacle's damage a blow does, so easy takes 60 percent and chaos the full amount. Practice and debug runs, which have no
level, take 100. Every result is a whole number with today's damages (animals 6 on easy, barriers 48). */
const int[] difficulty_damage_percents = {60, 70, 80, 90, 100};
/* Survival items by level (the item balance plan, dev, 2026-11-10, after a player ran an hour taking every hit): life
capsules, steel shields and health potions spawn at this percent of their _chance rates, easy to chaos, pairs' second
items too; debug runs at 100. Below these, taking every hit costs more than the items give back, at every level. */
const int[] difficulty_item_percents = {25, 20, 15, 10, 5};
/* How many shares barriers get in the obstacle pick, where every other type has 1 (the item balance plan, dev,
2026-11-10): half of them pass in other lanes, where their countdown doesn't play, so they come twice as often. */
const int barrier_weight = 2;
/* Combined obstacles (the combined obstacles plan, dev, 2026-11-11): a pair replaces this percent of obstacle spawns,
easy to chaos (debug runs at chaos's). The pairs, each also coming reversed (combo.nvgt), and the gap after a pair's
first part by its action, in ms: a jump, a crouch, a quick action (a lane switch, firing or one hand), and the wider gap
between a force field and an animal either way. */
const int[] difficulty_combo_percents = {5, 10, 15, 20, 25};
const string[] combo_firsts = {"projectiles", "force_fields", "force_fields", "mines", "barriers", "walls", "animals", "fake_doors"};
const string[] combo_seconds = {"spikes", "walls", "animals", "barriers", "projectiles", "barriers", "hazards", "mines"};
const int combo_gap_jump = 1200;
const int combo_gap_crouch = 600;
const int combo_gap_quick = 500;
const int combo_gap_hands = 1000;
/* Slides (the slides plan, dev, 2026-11-11): about one spawn in slide_chance is a slide, and it must also pass the
level's item_percent() (survival_roll()), so about 1 in 24 on easy to 1 in 120 on chaos; the debug choice "slides" makes
it 1 in 2 instead. A ride lasts a random slide_min_time to slide_max_time. */
const int slide_chance = 6;
const int slide_min_time = 2000;
const int slide_max_time = 4000;
/* Winds (the winds plan, dev, 2026-11-10 and 11): a wind closes in wind_speed_factor times as fast as a still obstacle
(moving toward you at half the belt's speed), moves one lane toward yours every wind_beat_time ms, and does wind_damage. */
const double wind_speed_factor = 1.5;
const int wind_beat_time = 750;
const int wind_damage = 5;
/* Ladders (the ladders plan, dev, 2026-11-12): each ladder has a random ladder_rungs_min to ladder_rungs_max rungs by level
(dev, after testing: 5 felt too short; 6 to 8 on easy up to 10 to 12 on chaos), the first taken as you step on; each
must come within ladder_rung_times of the last, by level from easy to chaos (practice and debug use easy's); a collapse
costs ladder_break_damage and a fall ladder_fall_damage, then the real wall's crash wall_damage. */
const int[] ladder_rungs_min = {6, 7, 8, 9, 10};
const int[] ladder_rungs_max = {8, 9, 10, 11, 12};
const double[] ladder_rung_times = {2000, 1750, 1500, 1250, 1000};
const int ladder_break_damage = 60; // a collapse (dev, 2026-11-12: 60 for a collapse, 40 for a fall)
const int ladder_fall_damage = 40;
// The least time between rungs by level (dev, 2026-11-12): sooner is rushing it, and you fall off.
const double[] ladder_rung_min_times = {200, 250, 300, 350, 400};
const bool ladder_grab_runup = true; // true: after a grab you run on to the ladder before climbing (the dev's choice, 2026-11-12, after trying both); false: the climb starts at the grab
const int ladder_wall_gap = 5;
// Floor breakers (the floor breakers plan, dev, 2026-11-13): a random floor_pieces_min to floor_pieces_max pieces by level, easy to chaos.
const int[] floor_pieces_min = {3, 4, 5, 6, 7};
const int[] floor_pieces_max = {4, 5, 6, 7, 8}; // steps from a ladder to its real wall (dev, 2026-11-12, after testing)
/* Vehicles (the vehicles plan, dev, 2026-11-13): closing vehicle_speed_factor times as fast as a still obstacle, a lane
toward yours every vehicle_beat_time; in your lane, bursts of vehicle_burst_shots shots vehicle_shot_gap apart, then
vehicle_burst_pause; each shot a tile every vehicle_shot_tile_time, vehicle_shot_damage if it reaches you in its lane; a
ram of vehicle_ram_damage; hp half a fake wall's (wall_spawn_hp()). */
const double vehicle_speed_factor = 1.5;
const int vehicle_beat_time = 1000;
const int vehicle_burst_shots = 5;
const int vehicle_shot_gap = 50; // 200 at first, then 50 (dev, 2026-11-13: "50ms was way better")
const int vehicle_aim_delay = 500; // lined up with you, it waits this long before a burst, so leaving its lane dodges it (dev, 2026-11-13)
const int vehicle_burst_pause = 2000; // 2000 at first, 1000 for a while, then 2000 again to give shooting room (dev, 2026-11-13)
const int vehicle_shot_tile_time = 50; // 30 at first, then 50 (dev, 2026-11-13)
const float vehicle_fade = 0.25; // a vehicle's shots fall off along the belt at a quarter of the belt's rate, so they carry (dev, 2026-11-13)
const float vehicle_engine_fade = 0.5; // its engine at half the belt's rate: 0.25 sounded too close as it appeared (dev, 2026-11-13)
const int vehicle_shot_damage = 5;
const int vehicle_ram_damage = 40;
const double vehicle_ram_range = 2; // within this many tiles of you a vehicle stops firing and rams (dev, 2026-11-13)
const int vehicle_min_hp = 25;
const int vehicle_max_hp = 250;
/* Trampolines (the trampolines plan, dev, 2026-11-11): like slides, one spawn in trampoline_chance and survival_roll();
worn pads trampoline_worn_percent of the time, belt-wide ones trampoline_belt_percent; a good pad's flight lasts
trampoline_air_time. */
const int trampoline_chance = 6;
const int trampoline_worn_percent = 50;
const int trampoline_belt_percent = 25;
const int trampoline_air_time = 2500;
/* Top speed by level (the difficulty scaling plan, dev, 2026-11-09): the step time where an endless run's belt stops
speeding up, 5, 6.7, 10, 13.3 and 20 steps a second. Every obstacle and item has joined by easy's 200. Debug runs keep
min_step_time, and Rush Hour can still go speedup_amount past the cap, never past min_step_time. */
const int[] difficulty_top_step_times = {200, 150, 100, 75, 50};
/* The schedule (Section 5, dev, 2026-11-05): on easy to insane, each of these types and items joins the mix once the
belt reaches its speed, one obstacle type per 50 ms mark, in order of the action it needs. Anything not listed is in from
the start: hazards, spikes and mines, health potions, life capsules and steel shields, and keys, which come before every
real door outside the schedule. Chaos has everything from the first spawn. */
const string[] schedule_types = {"projectiles", "force_fields", "animals", "walls", "ammo_packs", "fake_doors", "player_teleporters", "barriers", "powerups", "slides", "winds", "trampolines", "ladders", "floor_breakers", "vehicles"};
const int[] schedule_join_times = {450, 400, 350, 300, 300, 250, 250, 200, 200, 300, 200, 300, 250, 250, 200}; // vehicles at 5 steps a second (the vehicles plan, dev, 2026-11-13) // floor breakers at 4 steps a second (the floor breakers plan, dev, 2026-11-13) // ladders at 4 steps a second, with fake doors (the ladders plan, dev, 2026-11-12) // trampolines with slides (the trampolines plan, dev, 2026-11-11) // slides at 3.3 steps a second (the slides plan), winds at 5 (the winds plan), dev, 2026-11-11
const int chaos_level = 4; // difficulty_names' index of chaos, which ignores the schedule
/* The locks (Section 6, dev, 2026-11-05: "5 runs per level, and a user is required to reach at least 1 door"): easy is
always open, and each other level opens after this many counted runs on the level below. */
const int difficulty_unlock_runs = 5;
/* Timed runs (the timed run plan, dev, 2026-11-13), by level, easy to chaos: the countdown's start and the finish line in
seconds of running; each clean pass adds and each hit takes away (dev: "I want medium to be 6/5"); a level opens after
timed_unlock_runs completed timed runs on the one below; warnings as the countdown drops past these. */
const int[] timed_start_seconds = {60, 50, 40, 30, 20};
const int[] timed_finish_seconds = {300, 270, 240, 210, 180};
const int[] timed_pass_seconds = {7, 6, 5, 4, 4};
const int[] timed_hit_seconds = {5, 5, 7, 8, 10};
const int timed_unlock_runs = 3;
const int[] timed_warn_seconds = {45, 30, 15, 10, 5};
const int timed_warn_rearm_seconds = 10; // a warning plays again only after the clock climbs this far above it (dev, 2026-11-13) // highest first, so a drop past several says only the lowest (dev, 2026-11-13: "5, 10, 15, 30, 45")
// The clean passes that feed the clock: every obstacle got past the right way (combinations_cleared left out, since each part counts).
const string[] timed_pass_stats = {"hazards_jumped", "spikes_jumped", "mines_jumped", "projectiles_ducked", "force_fields_switched_off", "animals_scared", "barriers_dodged", "winds_dodged", "walls_broken", "real_walls_climbed", "fake_doors_broken", "real_doors_opened", "floor_breakers_repaired", "vehicles_destroyed", "vehicles_dodged"};

// Each spike swings on its own rhythm: a random swing time between these, picked when it appears (dev, 2026-11-02).
const int spike_swing_min = 500;
const int spike_swing_max = 1000;

/* A mine arms (light, then its ticking loop) mine_arm_lead_time before its countdown starts, at the current speed, never
under mine_arm_lead_min_tiles, so light always comes first and the countdown follows (dev, 2026-11-02): 1 tile ahead of
the countdown at 500 ms, 5 at 100 ms, 10 at 50 ms, giving light the same half second to finish at any speed. */
const int mine_arm_lead_time = 500;
const int mine_arm_lead_min_tiles = 1;

/* Lives and health (dev, 2026-11-03). Every run starts with starting_lives and player_hp health. Each blow (anything but
a hazard, which ends the run) does its obstacle's damage, to a worn shield first, otherwise to your health; at 0 health
you lose a life and start the next at full health, or the run ends on your last life. Extra damage past 0 is dropped.
These damages replaced the fixed life costs (spikes 1, mines 2, doors 3) and the shield-only damages. */
const int starting_lives = 1;
const int max_lives = 20; // a life capsule can't take you past this; capsules themselves are unlimited (dev, 2026-11-04)
const int life_capsule_min_lives = 1; // a life capsule gives a random min to max lives (dev, 2026-11-04: "between 1 to 2")
const int life_capsule_max_lives = 2;
const int debug_lives = 2; // source-only debug runs of a single type start with these; "all" uses starting_lives (3 until 2026-11-04)
const int practice_unlock_count = 5; // clean passes of a practice obstacle that open the next one; hazards open endless run too (the practice locks plan, dev, 2026-11-10: "just like the diff modes")
const int practice_hint_limit = 5; // hints per kind in each practice run, and the practiced choice's things before the closing line (the practice guidance plan, dev, 2026-11-12)
const int practice_unlock_hold = 3000; // a hint this soon after an unlock line waits its turn instead of cutting it off (ms, on runtimer)
const int practice_hint_together = 100; // hints this close together (ms, on runtimer: placed in the same moment) queue instead of cutting each other off
const int practice_rising_period = 5000; // a rising practice run speeds up every this many ms, twice an endless run's rate (the rising practice plan, dev, 2026-11-12)
const int practice_rising_top = 100; // and stops at 10 steps a second, the fastest practice speed
const int practice_lives = 1; // every practice run starts with this, and gets it back after each practice death (dev, 2026-11-09: 1, not 2; only debug runs get 2)
const int practice_shields = 1; // and with this steel shield in the inventory, none on the belt (dev, 2026-11-09: 1, not 2)
const int player_hp = 200;
const int spike_damage = 20;
const int mine_damage = 60;
const int forcefield_damage = 30; // the throw still happens
const int projectile_damage = 40;
const int wall_damage = 50; // crashing into a wall you didn't destroy
const int door_damage = 70; // crashing into any door, real or fake

/* Doors (dev, 2026-11-03). A real door marks each new door_section_ms of speed (450, 400 ... 50) and plays at pitch
100. A fake door plays at one of these pitches, never near 100, so it always sounds off. */
const int door_section_ms = 50;
int[] fake_door_pitches = {80, 90, 110, 120};
/* Wall hp scales with speed (dev, 2026-11-03): its center runs from wall_min_hp at start_step_time (500 ms) up to
wall_max_hp at min_step_time (50 ms), and each wall rolls a random hp within wall_hp_spread percent either side of
that center, never below wall_min_hp or above wall_max_hp. So 50 to 60 at the start, about 200 to 300 at 300 ms, and
400 to 500 at top speed. (It was a flat random 100 to 500, then 200 to 2000, then 20 to 2000; 50 to 500 since
2026-11-05, when guns couldn't break the fastest walls in time.) */
const int wall_min_hp = 50;
const int wall_max_hp = 500;
const int wall_hp_spread = 20;
/* Fake doors scale the same way with their own, tougher range (dev, 2026-11-05: "Doors are meant to be much stronger than
walls"; they shared the walls' hp until then): 100 to 120 at the start, about 400 to 600 at 300 ms, 800 to 1000 at top speed. */
const int door_min_hp = 100;
const int door_max_hp = 1000;

/* A projectile closes in this many times as fast as a still obstacle seems to, scaled with the belt's speed (dev,
2026-11-02): at 2 it starts as far beyond its meeting tile as you are before it, and flies at your own speed. */
const int projectile_speed_factor = 2;

/* Running into an active force field throws you this many tiles forward past it (dev, 2026-11-02). The gap after every
force field gets the same number of extra tiles, so the throw always lands on clear floor before the next countdown. */
const int forcefield_knockback_tiles = 5;

/* A force field can always be switched off within this long before it, at the current speed, even when its countdown is
shorter (dev, 2026-11-02, so top speed doesn't need mashing). At 50 ms that's the last 10 steps, at 100 ms the last 5,
at 200 ms the last 3; above 200 ms the countdown already lasts at least this long, so this changes nothing there. */
const int switch_min_time = 500;

/* Weapons (dev, 2026-11-02). Every hit's damage is the weapon's base damage (weapons.nvgt) times this, for all ten
weapons at once: 4 makes the bat 12 and the pistol 120 (dev, 2026-11-03, while testing walls; it was 2). */
const int weapon_damage_multiplier = 4;
// Each gun starts every run with this much loaded and in reserve; ammo packs refill the reserve.
const int gun_start_loaded = 50;
const int gun_start_reserve = 50; // was 250; lowered so ammo packs matter (dev, 2026-11-03)
/* The shortest gap between two swings (melee) or two pistol shots per Space press, and the machine gun's rate while Space
is held. Both press gaps were one shared 50 ms, too short for the weapon powerups to be heard (dev, 2026-11-04). */
const int melee_fire_gap = 200;
const int pistol_fire_gap = 100;
const int machine_gun_fire_gap = 100;
// Every weapon reaches this far ahead, turned into tiles at the current speed (dev, 2026-11-03).
const int weapon_reach_time = 2000;
// A gun's bullet moves one tile every this many ms, at any speed (dev, 2026-11-03); it travels weapon_reach() tiles.
const int bullet_tile_time = 30; // first 30, tried at 50, settled on 40 (dev, 2026-11-03), back to 30 (dev, 2026-11-05), so bullets stay ahead of you even at 50 ms steps

/* Ammo packs (dev, 2026-11-02). About one spawn in ammo_pack_chance is a pack instead of an obstacle. Opening one adds
a random ammo_pack_min to ammo_pack_max rounds to the reserve of the gun you're holding (dev, 2026-11-03; it was a
flat 50 to both guns), never above gun_max_reserve. */
const int ammo_pack_chance = 8;
const int ammo_pack_min = 5;
const int ammo_pack_max = 10;
const int gun_max_reserve = 200; // was 250 (dev, 2026-11-03); a reload still loads at most gun_start_loaded (50)

/* Shields (dev, 2026-11-03). About one spawn in shield_chance is a steel shield. A worn one starts at shield_hp and
takes each blow's damage (the <type>_damage values above) instead of your health; hazards ignore it. */
const int shield_chance = 16; // first proposed as 20 (dev chose 16)
const int shield_hp = 400; // first proposed as 100, then 200; 400 since 2026-11-04 (dev: "armor is twice as strong as you")

/* Life capsules and player teleporters (dev, 2026-11-03). About one spawn in life_capsule_chance is a capsule and one in
teleporter_chance a teleporter. A teleport moves you a random teleport_min_time to teleport_max_time of belt (in tiles
at the current speed), forward or back. */
/* Powerups (dev, 2026-11-03 and 4). About one spawn in powerup_chance is a powerup, and each lasts powerup_time. Their
effects: Slow Motion and Rush Hour shift the step by powerup_speed_ms; Moon Jump and Short Hop scale each jump height's
time; Long Crouch and Stiff Knees scale duck_time; Quick Swings and Rapid Fire scale a fire gap by powerup_fire_faster,
Clumsy Swings and Sticky Trigger by powerup_fire_slower; Sturdy Shield and Tough Hide scale damage to your shield or
health by powerup_damage_less, Brittle Shield and Soft Hide by powerup_damage_more. */
const int powerup_chance = 10;
const int powerup_time = 15000; // first 20000 (dev, 2026-11-04)
const int powerup_speed_ms = 50; // first proposed as 100 (dev chose 50)
const double moon_jump_factor = 1.5;
const double short_hop_factor = 2.0 / 3.0;
const double long_crouch_factor = 2.0;
const double stiff_knees_factor = 0.5;
const double powerup_fire_faster = 0.5;
const double powerup_fire_slower = 2.0;
const double powerup_damage_less = 0.5;
const double powerup_damage_more = 2.0;
// A powerup on the belt replays its sound this often, not looped (dev, 2026-11-04): ground ones every 300 ms, flight ones every 400 (the dev's final choice, after trying 500, 350, 250 and 500 for flight).
const int powerup_ground_sound_time = 300;
const int powerup_flight_sound_time = 400;
const int life_capsule_chance = 20;
const int teleporter_chance = 16;
/* Health potions (dev, 2026-11-04). About one spawn in health_potion_chance is a health potion, which heals a random
health_potion_min_percent to health_potion_max_percent of player_hp (10 to 20 of 200), never past full. */
const int health_potion_chance = 10;
const int health_potion_min_percent = 5;
const int health_potion_max_percent = 10;
// Lanes (dev, 2026-11-04): how far to the side the next lane over is heard, as a pan (100 is fully to one side).
const float lane_pan_amount = 50;
// The forward belt's pan per lane: the engine pans by x * pan_step / 125, so this makes one lane across lane_pan_amount (2026-11-05).
const float lane_pan_step = lane_pan_amount * 1.25;
// With HRTF on, a barrier one lane over sits this many units across per tile ahead: 1 is about 45 degrees to the side, two lanes about 63 (dev, 2026-11-05).
const float barrier_hrtf_spread = 1.0;
// A barrier in your lane does barrier_damage (dev: 80, the hardest blow).
const int barrier_damage = 80;
// How often, in percent, a barrier spawn is a pair in two different lanes instead of one (dev, 2026-11-04: "half the time").
const int barrier_pair_percent = 50;
// How often, in percent, an item spawn adds a second item of a random kind in a different lane (dev, 2026-11-05: the barriers' rule for items).
const int item_pair_percent = 50;
// Animals (dev, 2026-11-04; birds so far): an unscared animal that reaches you does animal_damage.
const int animal_damage = 10;
// Hands (dev, 2026-11-04): the second hand within this many ms of the first makes a clap instead of a woosh.
const int clap_window = 100;
const int teleport_min_time = 2000;
const int teleport_max_time = 5000;

// Music and ambience volume, in decibels: min_volume is silent-ish, 0 is full. The settings sliders show it as 0 to 100 percent. Home/End and Page Up/Down move by volume_change.
const int min_volume = -100; // -50 until 2026-11-08 (the volume sliders plan: "the ambience/music volumes should be able to go to -100")
const int learn_min_volume = -50; // the learn sounds menu's floor, unchanged
const int volume_change = 1; // 1 per press (dev, 2026-11-02)
const int music_start_volume = -20; // 80 percent at the start and after a settings reset (dev, 2026-11-09; full volume until then)
const int ambience_start_volume = -20; // 80 percent, the same
const int menu_music_start_volume = -20; // 80 percent, the same (form_menu.nvgt starts menumusvolume at it)
/* The ambience changes the way the ground does (the music and ambience plan, dev, 2026-11-06: "I like the 1 to 2minute
switch"): after a random ambience_min_time to ambience_max_time on runtimer, it crossfades over ambience_fade_time to
another random one, the old fading down to ambience_fade_floor decibels below your ambience volume as the new one rises. */
const int ambience_min_time = 60000;
const int ambience_max_time = 120000;
const int ambience_fade_time = 2000;
const int ambience_fade_floor = 40;
/* Environments (the environments plan's Section 2, dev, 2026-11-10: "I'd say 1 to 2 minutes"): with more than one
environment to go to, a run moves to a random different one every random env_switch_min_time to env_switch_max_time of
running time (runtimer, so pausing freezes it). The switch brings the new ambience, so the ambience timer above only
runs when there's nothing to switch to. */
const int env_switch_min_time = 60000;
const int env_switch_max_time = 120000;

/* The heartbeat (the heartbeat plan, dev, 2026-11-08): heart_start_bpm at start_step_time, rising in a straight line to
heart_max_bpm at heart_full_speed_ms: 5 + (500 - step time) x 150 / 350, about 4.3 bpm per 10 ms, so 155 at 150 ms, held there at any faster speed. A beat comes every
heart_gap_base - heart_gap_per_bpm x bpm ms (1950 ms at 5 bpm, 450 at 155).
(The breathing bands were taken out with the breath sounds, dev, 2026-11-08.) */
const int heart_start_bpm = 5; // 50 for a test on 2026-11-08, then back to 5 (dev: "5=500, and 150=200")
const int heart_max_bpm = 155; // reached at heart_full_speed_ms and held at any faster speed, powerups included (150 at 200 ms until 2026-11-08)
const int heart_full_speed_ms = 150; // the step time where the heart rate reaches heart_max_bpm
const int heart_gap_base = 2000;
const int heart_gap_per_bpm = 10;
